First reproduce the finding on this freshly based worktree and try to disprove
it. If it is stale, already fixed, incorrectly scoped, or not reproducible, do
not edit the repository and return a rejected proof below.

Keep the agent phase to four bounded responses so enough allowance remains to
implement the fix and write its proof. In the first response, read the evidence
files and locate/read the likely regression test in parallel; use at most one
targeted Grep or Glob for the named invariant or test. In the second response,
run at most one focused pre-edit reproduction and decide whether to reject or
fix. In the third response, batch the implementation and regression edits. In
the fourth response, write the JSON proof immediately. Do not read unrelated
whole files. Do not run tests, stash/revert the implementation, or simulate the
base checkout after editing: Hive independently runs the configured
fail-before/pass-after proof and broader validation.

If confirmed, make the smallest complete root-cause fix, not the smallest
one-line symptom patch. Audit sibling callers, input variants, and boundary
paths named by the invariant. Add or strengthen a targeted regression that
captures the original behavior. Use the finding's required validation key from
the operator-configured patrol commands. Do not supply command text or
self-attested before/after results. Hive will run that operator-configured command
on an isolated base checkout with the changed regular files you declare in
`regression_paths` overlaid, require a normal nonzero failure there, and run the
same command on your fixed worktree before broader validation. That base failure
must be a plain nonzero exit of the command itself — not a timeout, a
termination signal, or exit 127 — and its output must name at least one
declared regression file (by path or basename), or Hive rejects the proof. The
regression files may use any language or project-specific directory. If a declared file
also contains the fix, overlaying it will make the base command pass and Hive
will reject the proof. A cohesive multi-file repair is preferable to a special
case that leaves the same root cause reachable elsewhere.

List at most <%= max_audited_paths %> relative files you actually inspected in
`audited_paths`, and at most <%= max_regression_paths %> changed regular files
that carry the regression in `regression_paths`. These are agent-reported paths:
Hive validates confinement and changed/repository-file membership, not the claim
that you read them.

Required operator-configured validation key: <%= finding.validation_key %>

